THOUGHT: NullAway complains because the no-arg constructor doesn’t initialize the non-null field `resources`. The simplest fix is to initialize `resources` to a non-null dummy `ResourceData` instance in that constructor, ensuring all control-flow paths set it. I’ll modify the constructor accordingly and then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '70,74c\	    public SaveData() {
	      data = new ObjectMap<String, Object>();
	      assets = new IntArray();
	      loadIndex = 0;
	      this.resources = new ResourceData();
	    }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/particles/ResourceData.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -i "NullAway" -n new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

